**Business Document: Environmental Compliance and Equipment Management in Mineral Extraction**

**Date:** October 10, 2023  
**Prepared by:** Samantha Reed, Environmental Compliance Manager  
**Company:** GreenEarth Minerals Inc.  
**Location:** Fort Collins, Colorado  

GreenEarth Minerals Inc. is committed to sustainable practices in the extraction and processing of lithium from the Rocky Mountain Basin. Our extraction processes utilize state-of-the-art equipment, including the XLR-2000 Separator and Eco-Filter System, which significantly reduce environmental impact. This document outlines our compliance with environmental regulations and equipment management strategies.

**Extraction and Processing Overview:**

| Process Stage       | Equipment Used         | Compliance Standard     | Responsible Team         |
|---------------------|-----------------------|-------------------------|--------------------------|
| Lithium Extraction   | XLR-2000 Separator    | EPA Regulations 40 CFR 261 | Extraction Team          |
| Water Treatment      | Eco-Filter System     | Clean Water Act         | Processing Team          |
| Waste Management     | Eco-Compactor 5000    | Resource Conservation and Recovery Act | Waste Management Team    |

The Extraction Team, led by John Carter, collaborates closely with the Processing Team, managed by Clara Johnson, to ensure that all extracted materials meet the specifications required by our major client, Tesla, Inc. As per our contract with Tesla, we aim to deliver at least 5,000 tons of lithium per quarter, ensuring that our operations remain efficient and compliant.

Environmental compliance is monitored through our partnership with GreenTech Solutions, which provides regular audits and assessments to ensure adherence to all state and federal regulations. The latest audit conducted on September 15, 2023, confirmed that our operations are in line with the latest standards set forth by the Colorado Department of Public Health and Environment (CDPHE).

Furthermore, the Waste Management Team, under the supervision of Michael Lee, is responsible for minimizing waste through the Eco-Compactor 5000, which reduces processing waste by up to 70%. All teams engage in monthly training sessions to stay informed about the latest compliance requirements and equipment usage protocols.

In conclusion, GreenEarth Minerals Inc. strives to balance efficient extraction and processing with our commitment to environmental stewardship. Our continuous investment in advanced equipment and compliance training ensures that we remain a leader in sustainable mineral extraction practices.